<!-- ================================================
     THE STORY
     ================================================ -->
<section class="py-20 lg:py-28 bg-white">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5">
    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-5 gap-12 lg:gap-16">
      <div class="lg:col-span-2">
        <span class="accent-line"></span>
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.18em] uppercase text-gray-400 mb-4">My story</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl mb-5">From a print shop to a Google Ads account.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-3 space-y-5 text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">
        <p>From 2010 to 2012 I worked at a graphics company. In 2013 I opened my own — design and printing. Flyers, shirts, canvas, signs, vinyl wraps, stickers, invitations. If it could carry a logo, I printed it.</p>
        <p>That same year I moved to the United States, and I left the business behind. I started over at a manufacturing company, in a job that had nothing to do with design. I'm still with that company today — except now I'm in the marketing department. It took a while to get back to the work I actually love.</p>
        <p>Along the way the work changed shape. In printing, an <strong>impression</strong> is the mark the press leaves on the material. In digital marketing, an impression is one person seeing your ad. Fifteen years later I'm doing the same job I always was: making sure the right people see you, and that what they see is good.</p>
        <p>That's what AAA Impressions is. Everything I used to print for one business at a time, plus everything digital I've learned in the last five years — for local businesses here on the Treasure Coast.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

